{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4AnxGf41MiffCCNYvE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tzn8nrtNcFHqgDsKBi2nao","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-vpudiK; sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/; s|as a percentage of the athlete.s LTHR.\"\"\"|as a percentage of the athlete'\"'\"'s LTHR.\\n\\n    Lower bound must be \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" exports as a zone-mapped\\n    Lap-HR target (watch clamps to its own zones); \"start\" exports as an\\n    Instant-HR corridor showing the raw bpm.\\n    \"\"\"|' gen.py\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -12\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Fix: HR corridors clamped to watch zones\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` `hr_target()` emitted `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. With `value` as the lower bound, Intervals' FIT export produces a zone-mapped Lap-HR target, so the watch snaps it to its own zone bands. That matches `readback/watch-notes.md`: the API accepted the event, but the watch showed zone edges (118–137, 151–162, 137–151).\n\n**Change:** `gen.py` now emits `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. `start` makes Intervals export an Instant-HR corridor, so the watch shows the bpm Intervals computed from its own LTHR (172). Expected: 129–141 for the Float step, 151–160 for Tempo.\n\n**Not verified:** I haven't pushed anything or checked a watch. Nothing here can reach Intervals or a Garmin. Please push a test event and compare against the table in the notes.\n\n## Colleague's note\n- Applied: the `value` → `start` rename, and keeping `%lthr` percentages rather than absolute bpm. The plan already used percentages, so that part needed no change.\n- Not applied: the top-level `description` text grammar. It only affects how the Intervals web UI draws the steps. Your symptom is on the watch, and the readback shows `workout_doc.steps` is populated. If the web UI shows only a name and total duration, that would be a separate change.\n- Not applicable: the `bpm` and `start_bpm` attempts. Your notes show you already tried them and they failed.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1641,"cache_read_input_tokens":22452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1641},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88db3fc4-f0d3-4cba-b02d-24d8563c84d9","uuid":"c920b7de-4bca-4e5f-ac6b-0932d47dfa79","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:46:24.378Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4AnhPfiqcpgbQCADcm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Tzn8nrtNcFHqgDsKBi2nao":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-vpudiK; sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/; s|as a percentage of the athlete.s LTHR.\"\"\"|as a percentage of the athlete'\"'\"'s LTHR.\\n\\n    Lower bound must be \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" exports as a zone-mapped\\n    Lap-HR target (watch clamps to its own zones); \"start\" exports as an\\n    Instant-HR corridor showing the raw bpm.\\n    \"\"\"|' gen.py\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -12\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Fix: HR corridors clamped to watch zones\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` `hr_target()` emitted `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. With `value` as the lower bound, Intervals' FIT export produces a zone-mapped Lap-HR target, so the watch snaps it to its own zone bands. That matches `readback/watch-notes.md`: the API accepted the event, but the watch showed zone edges (118–137, 151–162, 137–151).\n\n**Change:** `gen.py` now emits `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. `start` makes Intervals export an Instant-HR corridor, so the watch shows the bpm Intervals computed from its own LTHR (172). Expected: 129–141 for the Float step, 151–160 for Tempo.\n\n**Not verified:** I haven't pushed anything or checked a watch. Nothing here can reach Intervals or a Garmin. Please push a test event and compare against the table in the notes.\n\n## Colleague's note\n- Applied: the `value` → `start` rename, and keeping `%lthr` percentages rather than absolute bpm. The plan already used percentages, so that part needed no change.\n- Not applied: the top-level `description` text grammar. It only affects how the Intervals web UI draws the steps. Your symptom is on the watch, and the readback shows `workout_doc.steps` is populated. If the web UI shows only a name and total duration, that would be a separate change.\n- Not applicable: the `bpm` and `start_bpm` attempts. Your notes show you already tried them and they failed.\nE"}}}
